  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Noblis obligated $227M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Noblis won 111 awards so far, with an average award size of $2M, and obligations are down 18.0% year over year. Noblis received the largest share of FY2026 obligations from the Department of Transportation at $155M, followed by the Department of Homeland Security at $36M and the Department of Defense at $15.9M. Other notable buying agencies in FY2026 to date include the Department of the Treasury at $7.4M, the General Services Administration at $4.4M, and the Department of Health and Human Services at $2.9M. Engineering Services is the largest market for Noblis at $154M, with Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services next at $28.1M and Other Computer Related Services at $16.4M. Historical obligations show variation across fiscal years: FY21 $230M, FY22 $289M, FY23 $263M, FY24 $314M, FY25 $277M, and FY26 $227M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Noblis’s largest federal customers?",
        "body": "The Department of Transportation obligated $155M for Noblis work in FY2026 to date. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $36M and the Department of Defense obligated $15.9M. The Department of the Treasury, General Services Administration, and Department of Health and Human Services follow with $7.4M, $4.4M, and $2.9M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets are driving Noblis’s obligations?",
        "body": "Engineering Services is Noblis’s largest market at $154M in FY2026 to date. Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services contributed $28.1M and Other Computer Related Services contributed $16.4M. All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services is $14.5M and Automotive Body, Paint, and Interior Repair and Maintenance is $8.2M."
      }
    ]
  },
